IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cma-types`
IMPORT `cma-definitions`
IMPORT `cma-offences`
IMPORT `cma-punishment`
IMPORT `cma-scope-procedure`
IMPORT `cma-goal`

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from ../source/CMA1993.txt; the
-- provision is on each group.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

`no effect` MEANS `Effect on programs or data` WITH
    `altered or erased the program or data` IS FALSE
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS FALSE
    `used the data` IS FALSE
    `caused the program to be executed` IS FALSE
    `was itself a function of the program` IS FALSE
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS FALSE
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS FALSE
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS FALSE

`displayed data` MEANS `Effect on programs or data` WITH
    `altered or erased the program or data` IS FALSE
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS FALSE
    `used the data` IS FALSE
    `caused the program to be executed` IS FALSE
    `was itself a function of the program` IS FALSE
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS TRUE
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS FALSE
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS FALSE

`ran a program` MEANS `Effect on programs or data` WITH
    `altered or erased the program or data` IS FALSE
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS FALSE
    `used the data` IS FALSE
    `caused the program to be executed` IS TRUE
    `was itself a function of the program` IS FALSE
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS FALSE
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS FALSE
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS FALSE

`added malware` MEANS `Effect on programs or data` WITH
    `altered or erased the program or data` IS FALSE
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS FALSE
    `used the data` IS FALSE
    `caused the program to be executed` IS FALSE
    `was itself a function of the program` IS FALSE
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS FALSE
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS TRUE
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS FALSE

GIVEN e IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Authority
`authority` e c MEANS Authority WITH
    `the person is entitled to control (or determine) access or modification of the kind` IS e
    `the person has consent from a person so entitled` IS c

`no authority` MEANS `authority` FALSE FALSE

GIVEN loss IS A NUMBER, med IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Impairment facts`
`impairment` loss med MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
    `an impairment to a computer or to the integrity or availability of data, a program, a system or information` IS TRUE
    `loss caused, in dollars, within one year after the offence` IS loss
    `a different loss threshold prescribed by the Minister` IS NOTHING
    `modifies or impairs, or potentially, medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care` IS med
    `causes or threatens physical injury or death` IS FALSE
    `threatens public health or public safety` IS FALSE

GIVEN u IS A `Protected use`, knew IS A BOOLEAN, warned IS A BOOLEAN, rebutted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Protected computer facts`
`protected` u knew warned rebutted MEANS `Protected computer facts` WITH
    `access to the computer was obtained in the course of the offence` IS TRUE
    `use` IS u
    `the accused knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the use` IS knew
    `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to the accused` IS warned
    `the contrary of the presumed knowledge is proved` IS rebutted

`not protected` MEANS `protected` `none of the s 11(2) uses` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a bank's server` MEANS `protected` `(c) communications infrastructure, banking and financial services, public utilities, public transportation or public key infrastructure` TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `s 8A presumption facts`
`presumption` a b c r MEANS `s 8A presumption facts` WITH
    `did the act for any gain, wrongful or not, realised or not, to anyone` IS a
    `did it knowing it is likely to cause wrongful loss` IS b
    `failed to take reasonable steps to ascertain the identity and physical location of the recipient` IS c
    `the contrary is proved` IS r

GIVEN k IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A BOOLEAN, steps IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Scam facts`
`scam` k o used steps MEANS `Scam facts` WITH
    `knew the purpose or use was a scam offence` IS k
    `obtained or retained it for a scam offence, or for supply for one` IS o
    `proved to the court it was used for a scam offence` IS used
    `the accused proved reasonable steps against its use for a scam offence` IS steps

`no scam` MEANS `scam` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A `Dealing`, use IS A BOOLEAN, supply IS A BOOLEAN, knew IS A BOOLEAN, conduit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dealing facts`
`dealing` d use supply knew conduit MEANS `Dealing facts` WITH
    `dealing` IS d
    `purpose: use in committing or facilitating an offence` IS use
    `purpose: supply or making available for use in an offence` IS supply
    `knew or had reason to believe it will be or is likely to be used for an offence` IS knew
    `merely provides network access, routing or connection services` IS conduit

`obtains` MEANS `(a) obtains or retains`
`supplies` MEANS `(b) supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available`

`hacking a payroll server` MEANS `s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` TRUE TRUE `displayed data` `no authority`
`selling a Singpass login` MEANS `s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`presumption` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (`scam` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Goal 1 — definitions (s 2)`

GIVEN e IS A `Device exclusion`
GIVETH A Device
`device` e MEANS Device WITH
    `is an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical or other data processing device, or a group of them` IS TRUE
    `performs logical, arithmetic or storage functions` IS TRUE
    `exclusion` IS e

#ASSERT `a computer` (`device` `not excluded`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`device` `(b) a portable hand-held calculator`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`device` `(a) an automated typewriter or typesetter`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`device` `(d) a device the Minister has prescribed by Gazette notification`)

-- s 2(2)(d) output, s 2(3)(a) executing a program: each is securing access
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `displayed data`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `ran a program`
#ASSERT NOT `secures access to a program or data` `no effect`
-- s 2(7)(b): adding data is a modification; merely displaying it is not
#ASSERT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `added malware`
#ASSERT NOT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `displayed data`

-- s 2(5): unauthorised only if neither entitled nor consented
#ASSERT `without authority` (`authority` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `without authority` (`authority` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `without authority` (`authority` FALSE TRUE)

-- "damage": loss of at least $10,000; $9,999.99 is not, unless another limb applies
#ASSERT `damage` (`impairment` 10000 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `damage` (`impairment` 9999.99 FALSE)
#ASSERT `damage` (`impairment` 0 TRUE)

#ASSERT `a credential in relation to the national digital identity service` `a biometric identifier (an image or video of the user's face captured through the service)`
#ASSERT NOT `a credential in relation to the national digital identity service` `something else`
#ASSERT `a scam offence` (`Penal offence` OF "Penal Code 1871 s 420(2)", TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a scam offence` (`Penal offence` OF "Penal Code 1871 s 420(1)", FALSE)

§§ `Goal 2 — the offences`

#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `hacking a payroll server`
-- with the owner's consent it is not "without authority"
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` TRUE TRUE `displayed data` (`authority` FALSE TRUE))
-- s 4: the intended offence must carry imprisonment of not less than 2 years
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `displayed data` (JUST (`Intended offence` OF TRUE, 2)))
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `displayed data` (JUST (`Intended offence` OF TRUE, 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `displayed data` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` TRUE `added malware` `no authority`)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 8: disclosure needs one of the three purposes
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 8A: selling for gain raises the presumption (s 8A(3)(a))
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `selling a Singpass login`
-- the presumption rebutted, and no knowledge found: no offence
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`presumption` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) FALSE `no scam`)
-- s 8A(4): reasonable grounds to believe it was for a lawful transaction in the user's identity
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`presumption` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE `no scam`)
-- not a user of the service
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`presumption` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE `no scam`)

-- s 8B(2): obtaining for no offence purpose is not an offence
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no scam`)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no scam`)
-- s 8B(3): supplying is an offence if the purpose is offence use, or if the supplier knew it likely
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `no scam`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no scam`)
-- s 8B(4): a mere conduit does not transmit
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `no scam`)

-- s 9 Example 1: A downloads and retains the list to report it to the police
-- (no offence purpose: s 9(2)); transmits it to B to inform B, not knowing it
-- likely to be used for an offence (s 9(3)): no offence on either limb.
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 9 Example 2: C passes it to D for B's investigation — no offence
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- but selling the list to fraudsters is
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))

#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 12: abetment carries the offence and its punishment
#ASSERT `is guilty of the offence itself, with its punishment` `by abetment`

§§ `Goal 3 — punishment`

-- s 3(1)(a) first conviction $5,000 / 2 years; (b) repeat $10,000 / 3 years; (2) damage $50,000 / 7 years
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` `hacking a payroll server` `, repeat:` FALSE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 5000 2 0
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` `hacking a payroll server` `, repeat:` TRUE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` `hacking a payroll server` `, repeat:` TRUE `, damage caused:` TRUE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 50000 7 0
-- s 11: a bank's server — $100,000 / 20 years in lieu
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` `hacking a payroll server` `, repeat:` FALSE `, damage caused:` TRUE `, protected computer:` `a bank's server` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 100000 20 0
-- s 11(3): a warning exhibited presumes knowledge; rebutted, the presumption falls
#ASSERT `a protected computer` (`protected` `(a) the security, defence or international relations of Singapore` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a protected computer` (`protected` `(a) the security, defence or international relations of Singapore` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 11 does not enhance s 4, s 8 or s 10
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` (`s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `displayed data` (JUST (`Intended offence` OF TRUE, 7))) `, repeat:` FALSE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `a bank's server` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 50000 10 0
-- s 5: $10,000 / 3 years; repeat $20,000 / 5 years
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` (`s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` TRUE `added malware` `no authority`) `, repeat:` TRUE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 20000 5 0
-- s 8A(1): no repeat limb; (5)(a) 12 strokes for an individual who knew of the scam
#ASSERT `the maximum punishment for` `selling a Singpass login` `, repeat:` TRUE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS `punishment of` 10000 3 12
-- not an individual: no caning
#ASSERT (`the maximum punishment for` `selling a Singpass login` `, repeat:` FALSE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` FALSE)'s `caning strokes` EQUALS 0
-- s 8A(5)(b): used for a scam, reasonable steps not proved — caning; proved — none
#ASSERT `the caning strokes for` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`presumption` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (`scam` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)) `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the caning strokes for` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`presumption` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (`scam` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)) `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS 0
-- s 8B(5A): obtaining for a scam; (5B) supplying knowing of a scam
#ASSERT `the caning strokes for` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`scam` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the caning strokes for` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`scam` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the caning strokes for` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`scam` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) `, an individual:` TRUE EQUALS 12
-- s 8B(5): repeat $20,000 / 5 years
#ASSERT (`the maximum punishment for` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`dealing` `obtains` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no scam`) `, repeat:` TRUE `, damage caused:` FALSE `, protected computer:` `not protected` `, an individual:` TRUE)'s `fine` EQUALS 20000

§§ `Goal 4 — reach and procedure`

GIVEN here IS A BOOLEAN, there IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A `Serious harm`
GIVETH A `Territorial facts`
`territory` here there h MEANS `Territorial facts` WITH
    `the accused was in Singapore at the material time` IS here
    `the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time` IS there
    `harm caused or significantly risked` IS h

`no harm` MEANS `no serious harm in Singapore`

-- s 13(3)(b): a hacker abroad, the server in Singapore
#ASSERT `the Act reaches the conduct` `hacking a payroll server` (`territory` FALSE TRUE `no harm`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Act reaches the conduct` `hacking a payroll server` (`territory` FALSE FALSE `no harm`)
-- (b) does not reach s 9; (c) serious harm does
#ASSERT NOT `the Act reaches the conduct` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)) (`territory` FALSE TRUE `no harm`)
#ASSERT `the Act reaches the conduct` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`dealing` `supplies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)) (`territory` FALSE FALSE `(b) disruption of, or serious diminution of confidence in, an essential service in Singapore`)
-- (d) s 8A and s 8B always
#ASSERT `the Act reaches the conduct` `selling a Singpass login` (`territory` FALSE FALSE `no harm`)

-- s 14: same provision, same computer, within 12 months
#ASSERT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2027 1 9)))
-- fork F2 as revised: the anniversary itself is within 12 months; the day after is not
#ASSERT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2027 1 10)))
#ASSERT NOT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2027 1 11)))
#ASSERT NOT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 5", "server A", (YMD 2026 2 10)))
#ASSERT NOT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server B", (YMD 2026 2 10)))
#ASSERT NOT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 3", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)))
-- order of listing does not matter
#ASSERT `the acts may be charged as one offence` (LIST (`Act charged` OF "s 7", "server A", (YMD 2026 6 1)), (`Act charged` OF "s 7", "server A", (YMD 2026 1 10)), (`Act charged` OF "s 7", "server A", (YMD 2026 12 31)))

#ASSERT `the courts that may try an offence and impose the full penalty` EQUALS LIST "a District Court", "a Magistrate's Court"
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` TRUE EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a compensation order may be made, convicted:` TRUE `, another's computer, program or data harmed:` TRUE
-- s 17(2): damages assessed at $8,000, $5,000 paid under the order: $3,000 remains
#ASSERT `the damages still recoverable in a civil claim, assessed at` 8000 `, compensation paid` 5000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the damages still recoverable in a civil claim, assessed at` 4000 `, compensation paid` 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `a police officer may arrest without warrant, reasonably suspected:` TRUE
#ASSERT count `provisions carried as text` EQUALS 3

§§ `The top-level goal`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, o IS AN `Alleged offence`, repeat IS A BOOLEAN, i IS AN `Impairment facts`, p IS A `Protected computer facts`, t IS A `Territorial facts`
GIVETH A Case
`a case` d o repeat i p t MEANS Case WITH
    `conduct on` IS d
    `alleged` IS o
    `participation` IS `as principal`
    `a second or subsequent conviction` IS repeat
    `the offender is an individual` IS TRUE
    `damage` IS i
    `protected computer` IS p
    `territory` IS t
    `prescribed as compoundable` IS FALSE

-- a payroll hack from abroad in 2026 causing $12,000 of loss: reached by s 13(3)(b), damage, $50,000 / 7 years
`the payroll case` MEANS `a case` (YMD 2026 3 1) `hacking a payroll server` FALSE (`impairment` 12000 FALSE) `not protected` (`territory` FALSE TRUE `no harm`)
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `the Act reaches the conduct`
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `the offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `damage within s 2(1)`
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `maximum punishment` EQUALS JUST (`punishment of` 50000 7 0)
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `the offence alleged` EQUALS "s 3"
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `an arrestable offence (s 19)`
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the payroll case`)'s `most that may be collected to compound` EQUALS NOTHING

-- the same hack, but nothing in Singapore and no harm there: not reached, no punishment
`the foreign case` MEANS `a case` (YMD 2026 3 1) `hacking a payroll server` FALSE (`impairment` 12000 FALSE) `not protected` (`territory` FALSE FALSE `no harm`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the computer misuse position for` `the foreign case`)'s `the Act reaches the conduct`
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` `the foreign case`)'s `maximum punishment` EQUALS NOTHING

-- conduct before 30 December 2025: refuses (fork F1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the computer misuse position for` (`a case` (YMD 2025 12 29) `hacking a payroll server` FALSE (`impairment` 0 FALSE) `not protected` (`territory` TRUE TRUE `no harm`))
#ASSERT (`the computer misuse position for` (`a case` (YMD 2025 12 30) `hacking a payroll server` FALSE (`impairment` 0 FALSE) `not protected` (`territory` TRUE TRUE `no harm`)))'s `maximum punishment` EQUALS JUST (`punishment of` 5000 2 0)
